  "label": "S3 job_create（含 3 条 rubric 准则；只写 PENDING 审批）",
  "tool": {
    "name": "recruitment_job_create",
    "description": "Create a job (requisition) in the business database and, when criteria are given, its first rubric version. Output carries R4 three-axis labels: provenance is computed from the tenant's synthetic marker (FIXTURE unless the tenant is explicitly declared non-synthetic; never hard-coded LIVE), trigger is MANUAL, and connection is NOT_CONNECTED (no external system is read or written).\n\nWHAT IT WRITES (one transaction)\n- recruitment.job: code is unique per tenant (omit code to auto-generate JOB-<YYYYMMDD>-<6 hex>).\n- job_version v1 with the JD text: description_md / requirements_md. A job_version is never UPDATEd; later edits append a new version. If you omit BOTH JD fields, the title is stored as a placeholder and the output says jd_source=TITLE_PLACEHOLDER (no fake JD content is invented).\n- If criteria are given: rubric_version v1 plus an approval row with status=PENDING.\n\nWHERE job_id COMES FROM / GOES\n- This tool returns job.id (a UUID). Every later step (applications, screening) references that UUID.\n- Read it back with recruitment_job_get(job_id=...), which resolves the current approved rubric.\n\nDEPARTMENT\n- Give department_id, or department_name (case-insensitive exact match), not both. Omit both to use the tenant's only department. If the tenant has several departments the call fails with INVALID_ARGS(DEPARTMENT_REQUIRED) and lists detail.known_departments.\n\n\ncriteria — EXACTLY 9 KEYS, ANY EXTRA KEY IS REJECTED\n{\"key\",\"label\",\"kind\",\"weight\",\"field\",\"operator\",\"value\",\"question\",\"notes\"}\n- key: ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{1,40}$, unique inside the version.\n- label: 1..200 characters.\n- kind: MUST_HAVE | NICE_TO_HAVE | DISQUALIFIER. At least one MUST_HAVE or DISQUALIFIER is mandatory; a version made only of NICE_TO_HAVE cannot decide anything.\n- weight: 0..1, and the sum over the whole array MUST be 1 (tolerance 1e-6). Weight is display/sort only; it never decides a verdict.\n- Mechanical criterion: field + operator + value together, or none of the three.\n  * numeric fields (operator GTE | LTE, integer value): timeline.covered_months_closed, work_experience.entry_count, education.entry_count\n  * boolean fields (operator EXISTS, value MUST be true): work_experience, education\n  * \"3 years of experience\" => field=timeline.covered_months_closed, operator=GTE, value=36 (unit = MONTHS, integer: 3 x 12).\n- Judgment criterion (no field/operator/value): question is mandatory, 1..500 characters, one answerable yes/no question.\n- FORBIDDEN as field: name, phone, email, protected.* (age / gender / marital status / native place / photo) and any field not listed above.\n\nDEGREES, INDUSTRY, SOFT SKILLS ARE NOT MECHANICAL\nThere is no degree / major / industry field. Express them as a judgment criterion with question, e.g.\n  {\"key\":\"bachelor_or_above\",\"label\":\"本科及以上学历\",\"kind\":\"MUST_HAVE\",\"weight\":0.5,\"question\":\"候选人是否具备本科及以上学历？\",\"notes\":\"学历不在机械判定白名单内，由人复核\"}\nNever invent a field name to make a requirement look mechanical.\n\nAPPROVAL IS A HUMAN ACTION\nThe rubric this tool writes is PENDING, not approved. Until a human approves it, recruitment_job_get answers NO_APPROVED_RUBRIC — that is the expected state, not an error. Never claim the rubric is approved and never approve on the user's behalf.",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "title": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Job title, 1..200 characters after trimming (e.g. \"后端工程师\")."
        },
        "code": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Stable job code, ^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,40}$, unique per tenant. Omit to auto-generate JOB-<YYYYMMDD>-<6 uppercase hex>."
        },
        "department_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Department UUID. Mutually exclusive with department_name. Omit both to use the tenant's only department (fails with DEPARTMENT_REQUIRED when there are several)."
        },
        "department_name": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Department name, case-insensitive exact match (1..200 chars). Mutually exclusive with department_id."
        },
        "description_md": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "JD body (markdown), at most 20000 characters. Omit description_md and requirements_md together to store the title as a placeholder JD (output job_version.jd_source = TITLE_PLACEHOLDER)."
        },
        "requirements_md": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Requirements section (markdown), at most 20000 characters."
        },
        "status": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Initial job status: DRAFT (default) or OPEN.",
          "enum": [
            "DRAFT",
            "OPEN"
          ]
        },
        "criteria": {
          "type": "array",
          "description": "1..50 rubric criteria. The object below has exactly 9 keys and no others. kind is MUST_HAVE | NICE_TO_HAVE | DISQUALIFIER (at least one MUST_HAVE or DISQUALIFIER). weight is 0..1 and the array MUST sum to 1 (tolerance 1e-6). A mechanical criterion gives field+operator+value together; a judgment criterion gives question instead. Allowed mechanical fields: timeline.covered_months_closed / work_experience.entry_count / education.entry_count with GTE|LTE and an integer value; work_experience / education with EXISTS and true. name / phone / email / protected.* are forbidden as field.",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "key": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Stable machine key, ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{1,40}$, unique inside the version."
              },
              "label": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Human label, 1..200 characters."
              },
              "kind": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "MUST_HAVE",
                  "NICE_TO_HAVE",
                  "DISQUALIFIER"
                ],
                "description": "MUST_HAVE | NICE_TO_HAVE | DISQUALIFIER."
              },
              "weight": {
                "type": "number",
                "description": "0..1 display weight; the sum over the array must be 1 (tolerance 1e-6). Weight never decides."
              },
              "field": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Mechanical field from the closed whitelist (timeline.covered_months_closed, work_experience.entry_count, education.entry_count, work_experience, education)."
              },
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "EXISTS",
                  "GTE",
                  "LTE"
                ],
                "description": "EXISTS (boolean fields) | GTE | LTE (integer fields)."
              },
              "value": {
                "oneOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "boolean"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "integer"
                  }
                ],
                "description": "EXISTS requires true; GTE/LTE require an integer (months for timeline.covered_months_closed)."
              },
              "question": {
                "oneOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ],
                "description": "Judgment criterion: one answerable yes/no question, 1..500 characters. Required when field/operator/value are absent (e.g. degrees, industry, soft skills)."
              },
              "notes": {
                "oneOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ],
                "description": "Optional explanation, at most 1000 characters; never used for a decision."
              }
            },
            "required": [
